    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0367" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.24/739: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France (Tuck) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-22T10:00:00+02:00">August 22, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1223. Department’s 507, August 17, 2 p.m. I have pressed Rochat<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d348-f1"/> on three separate occasions for a reply to our note
                    requesting <pb facs="0368" n="362" xml:id="pg362"/> the renewal by the French
                    Government of the assurance previously given and on the basis of which our
                    Government agreed to resume the shipment of supplies to French North Africa.</p>
                <p>Today Rochat informed me that I might expect his Government’s reply at an early
                    date probably tomorrow August 23.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d348-f1" n="37" xml:id="d348-f1-content">
                <p>Charles Antoine Rochat, Secretary General of the French Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
